How can I map a key to perform one action on a short press vs a long press?
Example: Pressing "o" will type an "o" on single press alone, while pressing and holding 
for more than 250 milliseconds makes a "6" (or a macro).

if_single(key(KEY_O), key(KEY_6), 250)

-----
This macro will type an 's' if the macro'd key is tapped, but if held, it performs a backspace AND hold the Left Shift.
As is, it is handy to correct a lowercase letter to an upper one; modify as needed for your use case.

key(s).if_tap( None, key(KEY_BACKSPACE).hold_keys(Shift_L))
